      "Certification exams — you can now choose, per exam, whether results are released to the student immediately or held for your review. A new “Hold results for my review” option in the quiz settings keeps the score and pass/fail hidden from the student when they submit (they see “Submitted — awaiting review”); you then open the exam's gradebook, review the attempt, and click “Release results” to reveal the score and award the certification if it passed. Leave the option off (the default) and results show the moment the student submits, exactly as before. Exams with written (short-answer) questions already waited for grading; this extends that hold to any exam you choose, even all-multiple-choice ones.",
      "Certification exams — students can retake an exam until they pass. By default an exam allows unlimited attempts, so a student who doesn't reach the passing score can simply take it again; set a “Max attempts” cap in the quiz settings only if you want to limit retakes.",
